.TH ORO-PATH-PATH 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:path/path \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:path/path'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Example usage: import { Path } from 'oro:path'
.PP
Notes \- URL\-aware joins: When the first component is a URL, subsequent components are applied to its pathname. An absolute component (starting with `/` or `\\\\` on Windows) resets the pathname to the origin root. Username/password/host are preserved. \- Windows specifics: \- Drive\-relative paths like `C:foo` are not absolute. \- Cross\-drive relative paths do not exist; `relative('C:\\\\a', 'D:\\\\b')` returns `D:\\\\b`. \- UNC roots (e.g., `\\\\\\\\server\\\\share`) are preserved by join/normalize/parse. \- Supported PathComponent inputs include strings, URL objects, and objects with `{ url }` or `{ pathname }`.
.SH REFERENCE
